.Dd November 19, 2026
.Dt PD_SPLIT.PY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pd_split.py
.Nd prefill on one llama-server, decode on another
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar prefill_url
.Ar decode_url
.Op Ar n_predict
.Op Fl -slot-file Ar slot_file
.Op Fl -json Ar path
.Op Fl -label-prefill Ar label
.Op Fl -label-decode Ar label
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
computes the KV cache of a prompt on one
.Xr llama-server 1 ,
saves it to a slot file, restores that file on a second
.Xr llama-server 1
and generates the answer there, without computing the prompt again.
.Pp
The script sends one long prompt (about 1900 tokens) for prefill only, saves
the slot, restores it on the decode server and generates the requested number
of tokens there.
Then it runs the whole request on each server alone and reports whether the
split output matches the decode server's own output.
A mismatch is reported with the first differing character, so a broken split
run can be traced without reading two whole answers.
.Pp
Both servers must be started with
.Cm --slot-save-path
naming the same directory (the slot file is written by one and read by the
other), with the same model and the same context size, and with one slot
.Cm -np 1 .
Slot 0 of each server is erased first and used for every request.
.Pp
The two URLs must be http(s) URLs, written as they are given.
The scheme is matched case-insensitively (RFC 3986), so
.Cm HTTP://host
is an http URL and is accepted.
A URL with another scheme, a URL with a space or a control character in it, a
URL that is not ASCII, a URL without a host, a URL with a query or a fragment
and a URL whose port is not a number are refused before the first request is
made.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -slot-file Ar slot_file
The slot file name used by the save and restore requests.
The default is
.Cm pd-slot.bin .
.It Fl -json Ar path
Write the results (timings, outputs, comparisons) to this JSON file.
.It Fl -label-prefill Ar label
The label for the prefill server in the printed lines.
The default is
.Cm "prefill server" .
.It Fl -label-decode Ar label
The label for the decode server in the printed lines.
The default is
.Cm "decode server" .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
The split run finished.
.It 1
The run failed.
One line
.Pq Li "pd_split.py: ..."
on stderr, never a traceback.
.It 2
The command line was wrong.
.It 130
The run was interrupted.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Prefill on the GPU and decode on the CPU:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pd_split.py http://127.0.0.1:18080 http://127.0.0.1:18081 128
.Ed
.Pp
The same run with another slot file, other labels, and the results written to
a JSON file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pd_split.py http://127.0.0.1:18080 http://127.0.0.1:18081 128 \e
	--slot-file slot-42.bin --label-prefill gpu --label-decode cpu \e
	--json pd-split.json
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr llama-server 1
